'''''Myosotis dubia''''' is a species of [[Myosotis|forget-me-not]] in the family [[Boraginaceae]]. It was previously considered a subspecies of the changing forget-me-not (''[[Myosotis discolor]]''), until recent genetic work discovered the two species to have different [[Ploidy|chromosome ploidy]], where ''Myosotis dubia'' was found to be diploid, while ''M. discolor'' was hexaploid.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Zonneveld |first=Ben |date=2019 |title=The DNA weights per nucleus (genome size) of more than 2350 species of the Flora of The Netherlands, of which 1370 are new to science, including the pattern of their DNA peaks |journal=Forum Geobotanicum |volume=8 |pages=24−78 |doi=10.3264/FG.2019.1022 |doi-access=free}}</ref> 

== Description ==
The plants are 15 to 65 cm tall with several side branches and spreading hairs that extend all the way to the top leaf.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |vauthors=Dirkse GM, Zonneveld B, Duistermaat H |date=2022 |title=Myosotis dubia Arrond. (Boraginaceae), Bleek vergeet-mij-nietje, in Nederland en Duitsland en hoe deze soort te onderscheiden van M. discolor Pers.(Veelkleurig vergeet-mij-nietje) |url=https://www.debastei.nl/sites/default/files/2022-08/2022_44_Myosotis%20dubia_GOR2022044001004.pdf |journal=Dutch Botanical Archives |volume=44 |pages=016–033 |eissn=2542-8578}}</ref> The [[inflorescence]] features small flowers coiled in a scorpioid pattern, where the petals start off pure white, changing to blue as they mature. The leaves follow an alternate arrangement, and are [[Glossary of leaf morphology|linear to oblong]] in shape.<ref name=":0" /> Each mature flower produces four [[Nutlet|nutlets.]]<ref>{{Cite book |title=The Illustrated Flora of British Columbia |publisher=British Columbia Ministry of Forests |year=1998 |isbn=0-7726-3685-0 |veditors=Douglas GW, Meidinger DV, Pojar J |pages=56}}</ref>

